sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant WD as Workers Dashboard
    participant CM as Configure Modal
    participant API as Backend API
    participant DB as Database
    participant TS as Tool Services

    U->>WD: View workers dashboard
    WD->>U: Display current workers & metrics
    
    Note over U, WD: User decides to create new worker
    U->>WD: Click "Add New Worker"
    WD->>CM: Open configuration modal
    
    Note over CM: Step 1: Choose Specialist Type
    CM->>U: Show specialist type options
    U->>CM: Select specialist type (e.g., Marketing)
    CM->>CM: Load default tools for selected type
    
    Note over CM: Step 2: Worker Details
    CM->>U: Show worker details form
    U->>CM: Enter worker name
    U->>CM: Enter description
    U->>CM: Select personality style
    U->>CM: Select response speed
    
    Note over CM: Step 3: Configure Tools
    CM->>U: Show tool categories
    U->>CM: Select "Communication & Email" tab
    CM->>U: Display available tools
    
    U->>CM: Toggle Mailchimp (connected)
    U->>CM: Toggle HubSpot (connected)
    U->>CM: Select Gmail (not connected)
    CM->>TS: Initiate Gmail connection
    TS->>U: OAuth flow for Gmail
    U->>TS: Authorize Gmail access
    TS->>CM: Connection confirmed
    
    U->>CM: Select additional tools
    U->>CM: Click "Create Worker"
    
    CM->>API: POST /api/workers/create
    Note over API: Validate configuration
    API->>DB: Save worker configuration
    API->>TS: Initialize tool connections
    TS->>API: Confirm tool setup
    API->>CM: Worker created successfully
    
    CM->>WD: Close modal, refresh dashboard
    WD->>API: GET /api/workers
    API->>WD: Return updated worker list
    WD->>U: Show new worker in dashboard
    
    Note over U, WD: Worker appears in dashboard with "Idle" status 